1
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:11,110
A survey asks 120 students how they travel to school.

2
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:12,380
Half of them walk.

3
00:00:12,430 --> 00:00:14,020
A quarter take the bus.

4
00:00:14,070 --> 00:00:16,830
The rest come by car or by bike.

5
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:21,770
A pie chart shows these parts of the whole as slices of a circle.

6
00:00:21,820 --> 00:00:23,890
A full circle is 360 degrees.

7
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:26,460
What angle shows the half who walk?

8
00:00:26,510 --> 00:00:30,200
Pause the video and work it out.

9
00:00:30,250 --> 00:00:31,830
Half of 360 is 180.

10
00:00:31,880 --> 00:00:36,220
The sector for walking has an angle of 180 degrees.

11
00:00:36,270 --> 00:00:38,920
It is half of the circle.

12
00:00:38,970 --> 00:00:40,890
A quarter of 360 is 90.

13
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:45,310
So the bus sector has an angle of 90 degrees.

14
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:48,780
Remember: a full turn is 360 degrees.

15
00:00:48,830 --> 00:00:49,900
Half is 180.

16
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:51,400
A quarter is 90.

17
00:00:51,450 --> 00:00:53,630
And 1 tenth is 36.

18
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:56,570
A pie chart is a circle, split into sectors.

19
00:00:56,620 --> 00:01:01,060
The angle of each sector is in proportion to its frequency.

20
00:01:01,110 --> 00:01:07,180
To find an angle: divide the frequency by the total, then multiply by 360.

21
00:01:07,230 --> 00:01:09,510
18 students come by car.

22
00:01:09,560 --> 00:01:13,790
18 divided by 120, times 360, is 54 degrees.

23
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:15,340
12 come by bike.

24
00:01:15,390 --> 00:01:17,740
That is 36 degrees.

25
00:01:17,790 --> 00:01:18,520
Your turn.

26
00:01:18,570 --> 00:01:19,760
The total is 72.

27
00:01:19,810 --> 00:01:20,930
1 group has 18.

28
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:23,410
What angle does that group need?

29
00:01:23,460 --> 00:01:26,910
Pause the video and try it.

30
00:01:26,960 --> 00:01:29,480
18 out of 72 is 1 quarter.

31
00:01:29,530 --> 00:01:33,090
A quarter of 360 is 90 degrees.

32
00:01:33,140 --> 00:01:36,740
You can also go from an angle back to a frequency.

33
00:01:36,790 --> 00:01:41,090
Divide the angle by 360, then multiply by the total.

34
00:01:41,140 --> 00:01:44,010
A pie chart shows 240 students.

35
00:01:44,060 --> 00:01:47,300
The sector for drama is 45 degrees.

36
00:01:47,350 --> 00:01:49,560
45 over 360 is 1 eighth.

37
00:01:49,610 --> 00:01:53,020
1 eighth of 240 is 30 students.

38
00:01:53,070 --> 00:01:53,790
Your turn.

39
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:55,100
The total is 180.

40
00:01:55,150 --> 00:01:57,870
A sector has an angle of 60 degrees.

41
00:01:57,920 --> 00:01:59,570
What is the frequency?

42
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:03,040
Pause the video and try it.

43
00:02:03,090 --> 00:02:05,520
60 over 360 is 1 sixth.

44
00:02:05,570 --> 00:02:07,770
1 sixth of 180 is 30.

45
00:02:07,820 --> 00:02:10,470
The frequency is 30.

46
00:02:10,520 --> 00:02:15,270
A waffle diagram is a grid of 100 squares: 10 rows of 10.

47
00:02:15,320 --> 00:02:18,000
Each square is 1 per cent.

48
00:02:18,050 --> 00:02:20,610
This waffle has 45 squares shaded.

49
00:02:20,660 --> 00:02:22,220
It shows 45 per cent.

50
00:02:22,270 --> 00:02:25,750
Waffles make percentages easy to count.

51
00:02:25,800 --> 00:02:27,110
Here is the method.

52
00:02:27,160 --> 00:02:30,030
Step 1: find the total frequency.

53
00:02:30,080 --> 00:02:35,180
Step 2: work out the degrees for 1 item: 360 divided by the total.

54
00:02:35,230 --> 00:02:38,220
Then multiply by each frequency.

55
00:02:38,270 --> 00:02:41,840
Step 3: draw each angle with a protractor.

56
00:02:41,890 --> 00:02:45,870
Step 4: check that the angles add up to 360 degrees.

57
00:02:45,920 --> 00:02:47,970
Add labels or a key.

58
00:02:48,020 --> 00:02:51,150
40 people choose their favourite sport.

59
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:56,110
16 choose football, 14 choose tennis, and 10 choose swimming.

60
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:59,260
Find the angles for a pie chart.

61
00:02:59,310 --> 00:03:01,450
360 divided by 40 is 9.

62
00:03:01,500 --> 00:03:04,850
So each person gets 9 degrees.

63
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:08,420
Football: 16 times 9 is 144 degrees.

64
00:03:08,470 --> 00:03:11,790
Tennis: 14 times 9 is 126 degrees.

65
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:15,810
Swimming: 10 times 9 is 90 degrees.

66
00:03:15,860 --> 00:03:20,850
Check: 144 plus 126 plus 90 is 360.

67
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:25,830
A waffle diagram has 28 squares shaded, for people who own a pet.

68
00:03:25,880 --> 00:03:27,520
350 people were asked.

69
00:03:27,570 --> 00:03:29,530
How many own a pet?

70
00:03:29,580 --> 00:03:32,570
28 squares means 28 per cent.

71
00:03:32,620 --> 00:03:34,770
0.28 times 350 is 98.

72
00:03:34,820 --> 00:03:37,740
So 98 people own a pet.

73
00:03:37,790 --> 00:03:39,810
School A has 600 students.

74
00:03:39,860 --> 00:03:43,710
On its pie chart, the sport sector is 60 degrees.

75
00:03:43,760 --> 00:03:45,780
School B has 240 students.

76
00:03:45,830 --> 00:03:48,330
Its sport sector is 120 degrees.

77
00:03:48,380 --> 00:03:52,620
Which school has more students who chose sport?

78
00:03:52,670 --> 00:03:56,140
School A: 60 over 360 is 1 sixth.

79
00:03:56,190 --> 00:04:00,000
1 sixth of 600 is 100 students.

80
00:04:00,050 --> 00:04:03,000
School B: 120 over 360 is 1 third.

81
00:04:03,050 --> 00:04:05,650
1 third of 240 is 80 students.

82
00:04:05,700 --> 00:04:10,890
School A has more, even though its sector is smaller.

83
00:04:10,940 --> 00:04:13,600
2 pie charts show favourite sports.

84
00:04:13,650 --> 00:04:18,550
Class A has 20 students, and its football sector is 180 degrees.

85
00:04:18,600 --> 00:04:23,430
Class B has 40 students, and its football sector is 90 degrees.

86
00:04:23,480 --> 00:04:25,130
Here is Dev's working.

87
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:27,850
Which line goes wrong first?

88
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:28,990
Line 2 is wrong.

89
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:32,040
A pie chart shows proportions, not numbers.

90
00:04:32,090 --> 00:04:34,300
You must use the totals.

91
00:04:34,350 --> 00:04:35,830
Half of 20 is 10.

92
00:04:35,880 --> 00:04:37,810
A quarter of 40 is 10.

93
00:04:37,860 --> 00:04:41,520
The 2 classes have the same number.

94
00:04:41,570 --> 00:04:45,390
A pie chart of the air you breathe has 1 huge sector.

95
00:04:45,440 --> 00:04:48,640
About 78 per cent of air is nitrogen.

96
00:04:48,690 --> 00:04:50,690
About 21 per cent is oxygen.

97
00:04:50,740 --> 00:04:55,560
All the other gases together make up only about 1 per cent.

98
00:04:55,610 --> 00:05:01,820
On a waffle diagram, that is 78 squares, 21 squares, and just 1 square.

99
00:05:01,870 --> 00:05:03,140
One last question.

100
00:05:03,190 --> 00:05:06,010
A waffle diagram has 27 squares shaded.

101
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:08,140
What percentage does it show?

102
00:05:08,190 --> 00:05:11,520
Pause the video and answer.

103
00:05:11,570 --> 00:05:12,440
27 per cent.

104
00:05:12,490 --> 00:05:16,590
On a waffle diagram, each square is 1 per cent.

105
00:05:16,640 --> 00:05:23,590
To remember: the angle on a pie chart is the frequency, divided by the total, times 360.

106
00:05:23,640 --> 00:05:28,670
The frequency is the angle, divided by 360, times the total.

107
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:31,380
A waffle diagram has 100 squares.

108
00:05:31,430 --> 00:05:33,820
Each one is 1 per cent.

109
00:05:33,870 --> 00:05:35,870
Pie charts show proportions.

110
00:05:35,920 --> 00:05:39,710
Check the totals before you compare 2 charts.

111
00:05:39,760 --> 00:05:45,110
Great work! Now practise lesson 16.3 on Camday.
